  "wikitext": "{{Named item|Rune Arm\n  | name                     = [[Corruption of Nature]]\n  | reqtrait                 = [[Rune Arm Use|Artificer Rune Arm Use]]\n  | minlevel                 = 17\n  | durability               = 225\n  | material                 = Wood\n  | hardness                 = 20\n  | quest                    = Outbreak\n  | chest                    = End chest\n  | end reward               = \n  | turn in                  = \n  | basevalue                = 12,050 pp\n  | weight                   = 0.25 lbs\n  | bind                     = {{Bind|BtC|BoE}}\n  | spell                    = Acid Shot\n  | target                   = Foe, Directional, Breakable\n  | school                   = Evocation\n  | sr                       = no\n  | spell desc               = Fires a missile of acid that corrodes your enemies.  At higher charge levels multiple projectiles are fired in a spray. Opponents struck by a projectile receive a Fortitude save for half damage.\n  | max charge               = 4\n  | imbue                    = Acid IV\n  | imbue die                = 2d8\n  | imbue dmg                = acid\n  | food                     = true\n  | enhancements             = \n* [[Acid Shot]]\n* {{SpellPower|Corrosion|84}}\n* {{SpellPower|Potency|56}}\n* {{Rough Hide|4}}\n  | craftable rune arm       = no\n  | epic                     = no\n  | crafting                 = <!--none-->\n  | craftingupgrade          = <!--What item can be upgraded to-->\n  | craftingnotes            = <!--Any notes about the craftable item-->\n  | pic                      = Acid Shot icon.png\n  | picdesc                  = Corruption of Nature (Level 17).png\n  | description              = This magical device, found in Eveningstar's hospital, seems to somehow have been altered by the magical plague afflicting the villagers. When worn by an Artificer capable of channeling energy through it, it infects them with a benign version of the disease, temporarily toughening th